WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:01.310
Part four.

00:00:01.310 --> 00:00:03.148
Variables and logic.

00:00:04.833 --> 00:00:08.551
A recording always types the same name and the same address.

00:00:08.551 --> 00:00:10.488
Variables make it flexible.

00:00:11.033 --> 00:00:15.315
The variable table lives in the Tools tab and is shared by every scenario.

00:00:15.315 --> 00:00:19.282
Add customer, a static variable, set to Anna Tran.

00:00:19.467 --> 00:00:24.343
Add houseNo as a random value: three digits, different on every run.

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:35.962
There's also Pick, one value at random from a list, and Fallback, which tries values in turn.

00:00:35.967 --> 00:00:42.643
Back in the scenario, edit the name step to use ${customer}, and the address to ${houseNo} Lake Road.

00:00:53.867 --> 00:00:55.394
Next, Read DOM.

00:00:55.394 --> 00:01:00.400
It reads the order number off the page while the test runs, and saves it into orderId.

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:04.794
Copy the text as it reads on the page, and put ${orderId} on the part to keep.

00:01:10.467 --> 00:01:15.993
Then use it again: open My orders, and check that the order we just read is listed there.

00:01:34.233 --> 00:01:35.817
Last, a Condition.

00:01:35.817 --> 00:01:39.134
If we're already signed in, there's no need to sign in again.

00:01:39.134 --> 00:01:41.914
Insert a Condition right after the sorting steps.

00:01:41.933 --> 00:01:44.930
The check: the greeting still says Not signed in.

00:01:44.930 --> 00:01:47.709
When it holds, the sign-in steps run.

00:01:47.709 --> 00:01:49.822
When it does not, they are skipped.

00:01:59.967 --> 00:02:00.873
Let's run it.

00:02:00.873 --> 00:02:07.123
We're signed in, so the sign-in is skipped, the name comes from the variable, and the house number is random.

00:02:13.133 --> 00:02:15.727
And the order we just placed shows up in My orders.

00:02:15.727 --> 00:02:16.662
Passed.

00:02:19.933 --> 00:02:25.660
Variables open the door to something bigger: running one scenario against a whole table of data.

00:02:25.660 --> 00:02:26.821
That's next.
